**Key:** Kind.5,unkind.3,change.2; utilities20 and24. theta=.1<rho=.4,so unkind weight remains positive. Utility difference-.2(20)=-4; kindness does not raise every fixed pair. Reciprocity treatment-dependence differs from unconditional positive weights and payoff inequality. Efficiency existing-model half-total gives16 versus19,prefers total38; no full separate model or one-transfer identification. Sequential trustee observes prior transfer; simultaneous player relies on belief; no quantitative reciprocity formula/rate for that game supplied. Here q=1 labels kind treatment, q=−1 misbehavior, and theta>0 is the sensitivity to treatment.

